les persist between calls: activate a virtualenv or export once, not before every command.\n\nUse read_file, search_files, patch and write_file instead of cat/head/tail, grep/find/ls, sed/awk and echo/heredoc. Output is auto-truncated with the full text saved to a file; never pipe through head/tail to shorten it.\n\nForeground (default) returns as soon as the command finishes. To wait a fixed time, run the wait in the foreground; never background a sleep or polling loop. Background is only for commands that must keep running after this call returns; health-check a server in a separate call and manage jobs with process_manage. When a command changes directory, trust the result's \"cwd\" instead of prefixing later commands with cd.\n","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"command":{"type":"string","description":"The shell command to execute"},"background":{"type":"boolean","description":"Keep running after this call returns; returns a session_id.","default":false},"timeout":{"type":"integer","description":"Max seconds (default 180, foreground max 600). Finishing early returns at once, so set it generously. Above 600s the command runs as a tracked background process with notify_on_complete=true (the result says so; do not re-run it).","minimum":1},"workdir":{"type":"string","description":"Absolute working directory for this command only."},"pty":{"type":"boolean","description":"With background=true: pseudo-terminal for interactive CLIs (REPLs, coding agents); drive it with process_manage write/submit. Local backend only.","default":false},"notify":{"description":"With background=true. true: one notification on exit; use it for anything that ends (builds, tests, deploys), or the job runs silently. ['pattern', ...]: notify when a line matches, only for one-shot readiness on processes that never exit; rate-limited. Omit for servers/daemons.","anyOf":[{"type":"boolean"},{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"}}]},"heartbeat":{"type":"integer","minimum":0,"default":0,"description":"With background=true: also notify every N seconds (min 60) with new output; quiet ticks are skipped. For bounded jobs you must react to mid-run, never servers. Implies notify=true; 0 = off."},"persist_on_release":{"type":"boolean","default":false,"description":"With background=true: survive session end, /new, compression and other cleanup (not host exit). Only for jobs the user explicitly wants to outlive the conversation."}},"required":["command"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"tool_search","description":"Search 1 additional tools that are loaded on demand. Send one keyword query per capability you need; returns matching tool names and descriptions. Then `tool_describe` loads schemas and `tool_call` invokes. Tools already in your tool list need no search.\n\nEvery tool listed below exists: never call it unavailable, and go straight to `tool_describe` when you see the exact name.\n\nDeferred tool catalog (call schemas via `tool_describe`, invoke via `tool_call`):\nterminal tools (1):\n- process_manage: Poll, wait on, or kill background terminal processes (from…","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"queries":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"One query per capability: service + action + object keywords (e.g. ['gmail send email', 'github create issue']), never a question; every word must match tool text. Searched in parallel."},"limit":{"type":"integer","description":"Max matches per query (default 5)."}},"required":["queries"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"tool_describe","description":"Load the full JSON schemas for tools returned by `tool_search`. Required before `tool_call` if a tool's parameters are unknown. Batch every schema you need into one call.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"names":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"string"},"description":"Exact tool names (as returned by tool_search). A single string is accepted and treated as one name."}},"required":["names"]}}},{"type":"function","function":{"name":"tool_call","description":"Invoke deferred tools: `calls` is an array of {name, arguments}, one entry per invocation (batch independent calls; results come back in order). Arguments match the schema from `tool_describe`; approvals and hooks apply as usual.","parameters":{"type":"object","properties":{"calls":{"type":"array","items":{"type":"object","properties":{"name":{"type":"string","description":"Exact tool name to invoke."},"arguments":{"type":"object","description":"Arguments matching the tool schema."}},"required":["name","arguments"]},"description":"One or more independent deferred tool invocations."}},"required":["calls"]}}}]}